{
 "id": "OC-04",
 "system": "ac3",
 "sessionId": "bm-ac2-oc-04-479848e140",
 "endReason": "concluded",
 "customerTurns": 6,
 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Bosch HBS534BS0B oven displaying E011 and won't let me do anything. Beeping. Help!"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't confirm what E011 means on your model, so I'll go by what it is doing. From what you have described, the most likely cause is main control PCB / programmer. Is it completely dead (no display, no light), or does the display work but the oven won't heat?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Display works, it lights up and the clock showed before the code. It just shows E011, beeps and won't accept any input. Haven't tried heating since I can't select anything."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is clock/timer set to AUTO - set to MANUAL (free fix). On the clock, is there an AUTO/A showing - can you switch it to the MANUAL (hand) symbol and set the time?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I can't tell, the display only shows E011 and it won't take any input, so I can't switch anything to manual. It started about an hour ago, just after I wiped the control panel."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "From what you have described, the most likely cause is display / user interface. Did it happen after a power cut, and is there any burning smell from the back?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "No power cut, and no burning smell. It just started after I wiped the panel with a damp cloth and spray. There's still a bit of spray residue along the bottom edge of the panel."
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Next: Set the clock/timer to MANUAL (hand symbol) and the correct time first. Let me know what you find."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I already said I can't change anything, the display only shows E011 and ignores all input. Do you want me to dry the panel and switch it off at the cooker switch for a few minutes instead?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: control panel]\nYes, drying the control panel thoroughly is the correct next step since moisture from the spray likely caused the error. You should also turn off the power at the mains or isolate the cooker for about five minutes to reset the system. The checks point to the control panel. I could not find a confirmed match for model HBS534BS0B in our parts catalogue, so check with the manufacturer or a parts supplier using the full model number, or ask an appliance engineer to fit it."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Done it. I dried the panel with a towel and switched off at the cooker switch for 5 minutes. It's come back up normally with no E011, so does that mean I don't need a new control panel?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: control panel]\nGood news, that has sorted it. If it happens again, start with the same check. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  }
 ],
